			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Decouple console log capture from debug server\n\nSeparate the JavaScript console log interception logic into `WindowBuild.rs` and remove it from `WebkitServer.rs`. The window builder now injects a script on page load to populate `window.__MOUNTAIN_DEBUG_CONSOLE` when `DEBUG_SERVER=1` is set, ensuring logs are captured before the TCP server initializes.\n\nRefactor `WebkitServer.rs` to rely on the injected JavaScript buffer instead of the Tauri `ConsoleEvent` listener. This eliminates the dependency on the internal Tauri console event API for log retrieval, allowing the HTTP server to simply query the DOM via `eval`.\n\nUpdate the request handling to support a new GET `/eval` endpoint for arbitrary script execution, replacing the removed `/dom` endpoint. Consolidate error handling and improve type safety using `once_cell::sync::Lazy` for global window storage and `BufReader` for HTTP parsing.",
			"SHA": "fd6648d17f6c0f7846eb45b9080b999506e186dc"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-14T21:16:54Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1491,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Introduce HTTP debug server for WKWebView inspection\n\nImplement a native debug server in `Source/Binary/Debug/WebkitServer.rs` to facilitate automated inspection of the native WKWebView instance on macOS. This component runs a lightweight HTTP server on `127.0.0.1:9933` (configurable) when `DEBUG_SERVER=1` is set, exposing endpoints for JavaScript evaluation, DOM querying, iframe enumeration, and console log retrieval.\n\nThe implementation installs a console event listener on the Tauri `WebviewWindow` to capture logs and spawns a background thread to handle incoming TCP connections. New routes include `GET /console`, `GET /dom`, `GET /iframes`, and `POST /execute`, allowing external tools or scripts to interact with the editor's runtime state.\n\nIntegrate the module into `Source/Binary/Debug/mod.rs` and invoke `WebkitServer::install` within `Source/Binary/Main/AppLifecycle.rs` after window creation. This complements the existing conditional devtools flag by providing programmatic access to the WebView for advanced debugging scenarios.",
			"SHA": "f14f21a072eaf20ed73ec9d69cb6da22c75fe3a0"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-14T18:38:50Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1490,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Enable conditional WKWebView inspection in debug builds\n\nAdd a conditional check in `Source/Binary/Build/WindowBuild.rs` to enable the `devtools` flag for the Tauri `WindowBuilder` when running in `debug_assertions` mode and the `Inspect` environment variable is set to a non-empty, non-zero value.\n\nThis modification allows external inspection tools (such as Safari Web Inspector or MCP) to attach to the native WKWebView instance on macOS during development, facilitating deep debugging of the editor's UI layer. The change preserves the existing behavior of disabling decorations on non-macOS platforms while introducing a gated mechanism for developer tooling on macOS.\n\nThe implementation leverages Wry's underlying `devtools` configuration to expose the native inspection interface only when explicitly requested.",
			"SHA": "6e51ac8b9e213cd70f7a379fd3d3ba091f41e54f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-14T16:50:21Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1490,
				4
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Reorder resources block and fix documentation links\n\nCorrect the ordering of files within the Tauri `resources` configuration in `tauri.conf.json` to group JavaScript bootstrap files prior to static assets and configuration manifests. This restores the logical dependency sequence expected during the application bundle initialization process.\n\nUpdate GitHub documentation URLs in `README.md` and `Documentation/GitHub/NamingConventions.md` from the legacy `blob` path to the canonical `tree` path, ensuring links correctly resolve to directory listings and file views on the `Current` branch.\n\nAlign dash formatting in `Source/Binary/Build/Scheme.rs` comments to use standard hyphens instead of en-dashes for code path descriptions.\n\nThese changes ensure consistent configuration loading and accurate external documentation references.",
			"SHA": "53fdb1751c9017d8a5dcc41e9007e44d52464cc2"
